  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 455 AM EDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nThe extended periods begin with a large high pressure ridge \ncentered over the northern Gulf keeping north and central GA warm \nand dry. Temperatures Tue through Fri will be in the 80s to near 90s \nwith lows in the 50s to near 60. This ridge stays entrench across \nthe southeastern U.S. through much of next week but it does slowly \nweaken allowing decent moisture return by Thu/Fri. Not expecting any \nprecip chances through day 7 but we will begin to see some increased \ncloud cover by Thu/Fri.\n\nBy next weekend, some of the model runs are beginning to indicate \nthe possibility for a strong cold front to push down from the north \nthat will bring fall back into the region.",
